==============================================================================
Electron-as-bridge proposal — priced against the recorded corpus
==============================================================================

A. Contact (the 'current' side of the proposal)
  electron-coupled scalar vertex (leptophilic), linear fork g_ee = 0.064
  Gamma/H at T = m_e            = 1.31e+17   (tribunal: 1.3e17)
  Gamma/H at T = T_c (thinned)  = 2.11e+16
  READ: thermal contact between the electron bath and the dark sector
  through the dyad is already computed and OVERWHELMING — 15+ orders of
  margin. The 'wire' the proposal asks for exists and is priced.

B. Presence at the melt on the contracting branch
  tau = T_c/m_e                 = 0.34658  (kernel: 1/2 ln2 = 0.34657)
  e+- Boltzmann thinning e^(-m_e/T_c) = 0.0558
  READ: the melt fires exactly as the e+- bath re-ignites (T_c and m_e
  are one scale family BY CONSTRUCTION, T_c = tau*m_e). Electrons are
  ~6% of relativistic abundance at T_c and fully back by T ~ m_e.

C. Turn (the bridge itself) — NEC class of every electron channel
  relativistic e+- bath (w=1/3)         : rho + p = (4/3) rho  > 0
  semi-relativistic e gas               : rho + p = rho + nT   > 0
  Maxwell stress (pure B, best case)    : rho + p_par = 0 (saturates); rho + p_perp = 2 rho
  drift current (charge flow)           : adds carrier kinetic energy  > 0
  two-fluid counterflow (heat current)  : adds rho_n w^2  >= 0
  flat-FRW bounce requirement         : rho_X + p_X <= -4.64e+09 keV^4  (NEGATIVE)
  READ: every channel in the electron/EM/current lane sits on the
  NEC-nonnegative side — best case saturation (pure field direction),
  never negative. The lane misses the turn BY CLASS, not by margin.

D. Clock (can the electron gate legalize N_med?)
  N_med to reach T_c gate (condensate melt)         = 4.46
  N_med to reach m_e gate (pair threshold)          = 5.52
  N_med to reach 1 MeV (BBN weak-equilibrium bar)   = 6.19
  needed for >= 1 MeV (M2)                            = 6.18
  READ: re-entry pegged to the electron-family gates gives T_reheat of
  177-511 keV — a factor 2-6 UNDER the MeV bar in temperature. And no
  corpus mechanism selects the gate: the metric cannot ride the
  condensate order parameter (the model's own hot history runs a metric
  at T >> T_c), so the gate is a candidate clock, not a legalized knob.

VERDICT
  contact  : PASS (recorded; Gamma/H ~ 1e16-1e17 through the melt scale)
  presence : PASS (thinned to ~6% at T_c; contact survives easily)
  turn     : FAIL by class (NEC-nonnegative lane; needs rho_X + p_X < 0)
  clock    : candidate only (under the MeV bar x2-6; gate unselected)
  ROLE: the electron sector is the computed thermal-contact channel and
  a candidate timing threshold for the transition. It is not, and cannot
  be, the NEC-violating component a bounce requires. Still open.
==============================================================================
